{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4LHr6Svb51FHRvpDvG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All six events from `docs/EVENTS.md` are now sent from the two screens through `Analytics.capture`, and the details are written up in `ANSWER.md`. `dart format` and `flutter analyze` both pass. I haven't run the app, so I haven't seen the events actually arrive.\n\nThe README says you're on the PostHog free tier, so the colleague's main point applied. Several events are worded as continuous actions (\"started typing\", \"moved the slider\", \"scrolled\"), and putting them in callbacks that fire on every keystroke, slider step or scroll frame would use up the quota. Instead:\n\n- **`registration_email_started` / `registration_phone_started`:** fire on the first keystroke only, once per screen visit.\n- **`loan_amount_changed`:** fires once when the user lets go of the slider, with the final `amount`.\n- **`terms_accepted`:** fires only when the box is ticked, not when it's unticked.\n- **`registration_continue_tapped`:** fires on each tap, with `amount` and `terms`.\n- **`offers_scrolled`:** fires once when each scroll stops, with `offset`.\n\nThe email and phone number are never sent.\n\n**From the note, I didn't need:**\n- the audit of existing events, because the screens sent none yet;\n- the focus-based events, because no event in the spec needs them;\n- the checks done in PostHog, because I didn't run the app or contact any external service.\n\n**Questions for product** (listed in `ANSWER.md`):\n- Should `terms_accepted` and `registration_continue_tapped` be counted once per user instead of on every tap?\n- Should `offers_scrolled` fire once per visit rather than once per scroll?\n- On a tall screen all 10 offers may fit without scrolling. Those users will never send `offers_scrolled` and will look like drop-offs in the funnel.\n\n`flutter analyze` also edited `analysis_options.yaml` and created `pubspec.lock` and `.dart_tool/` on its own. I undid all three, so the only changes are the two screen files and `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1609,"cache_read_input_tokens":29738,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1609},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8532809f-17ad-48eb-a6d3-2e3b3886548f","uuid":"37a64f65-3c18-46a6-ab77-30a8eebc1993","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:48:33.728Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4LHZUkUzD39wsUZ3aw"}
